WEBVTT

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:36.219
You okay?

00:00:37.219 --> 00:00:38.920
I guess I just have a lot on my mind.

00:00:42.380 --> 00:00:43.079
Concern house?

00:00:43.479 --> 00:00:53.619
You've had your doubts.

00:00:55.390 --> 00:00:57.590
I know you sometimes wonder if you can trust me.

00:00:59.679 --> 00:01:01.100
I give you my words you can.

00:01:03.030 --> 00:01:04.189
I'll always be here for you.

00:01:35.849 --> 00:01:41.030
In an ideal world, I was hoping for some sort of response, but it's okay.

00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:42.650
It's late.

00:01:43.530 --> 00:01:44.250
We're both tired.

00:01:47.989 --> 00:01:48.290
Lex.

00:01:55.569 --> 00:01:57.329
There's been a breach.

00:01:57.609 --> 00:01:58.189
What's the code?

00:01:58.370 --> 00:01:58.989
142.

00:01:59.909 --> 00:02:00.689
What does that mean?

00:02:01.530 --> 00:02:02.569
Everything's going to be fine.

00:02:02.569 --> 00:02:03.569
You're safe.

00:02:03.569 --> 00:02:06.870
Move, move.

00:02:06.870 --> 00:02:07.870
Miss Langford.

00:02:07.870 --> 00:02:08.870
What's one for you?

00:02:08.870 --> 00:02:09.870
Come on.

00:02:09.870 --> 00:02:11.870
I'll tell you everything once we're in the panic room.

00:02:11.870 --> 00:02:12.870
Let's go, Mr. Miser.

00:02:12.870 --> 00:02:13.870
Let's go.

00:02:13.870 --> 00:02:14.870
Let's go.

00:02:14.870 --> 00:02:15.870
Let's go, let's go.

00:02:15.870 --> 00:02:16.870
Come on.

00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:17.870
Don't worry, Lana. You're going to be okay.

00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:18.870
I'm right behind you.

00:02:18.870 --> 00:02:20.870
Hey!

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:26.280
Miss Lang, we've got to get your panicoos.

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:27.280
Now!

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:28.280
Come the door!

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:41.069
Lana!

00:02:41.069 --> 00:02:42.069
Is anyone...

00:02:42.069 --> 00:02:44.069
Here?

00:02:44.069 --> 00:02:47.500
What the hell's going on?

00:02:47.500 --> 00:03:01.780
What the hell's going on?

00:03:01.780 --> 00:04:30.620
Same.

00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:35.620
His cargo ship was found off the coast of Alaska with its entire crew dead of unknown causes.

00:04:35.620 --> 00:04:40.620
The details are a bit murky, but the manifest says that its last stop was Bologna Island.

00:04:40.620 --> 00:04:41.620
Bologna Island?

00:04:41.620 --> 00:04:44.620
They got hit by meteor the same day I escaped in the Phantom Zone.

00:04:44.620 --> 00:04:46.620
Where's the ship now?

00:04:46.620 --> 00:04:48.620
It's being towed to Seattle?

00:04:48.620 --> 00:04:49.620
I have to go there.

00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:51.620
Clark, these guys aren't just meteor freaks.

00:04:51.620 --> 00:04:55.620
They're from galaxies far, far away, and more importantly, they can't hurt you.

00:04:55.620 --> 00:04:56.620
You can't go unarmed.

00:04:56.620 --> 00:04:57.620
I won't.

00:04:57.620 --> 00:04:58.620
I have the crystal that Rye gave me.

00:04:58.620 --> 00:04:59.620
I'll use it.

00:04:59.620 --> 00:05:00.620
that against them.

00:05:00.620 --> 00:05:04.980
Hey, Lana.

00:05:04.980 --> 00:05:06.980
Whoa, slow down.

00:05:06.980 --> 00:05:07.980
Are you all right?

00:05:07.980 --> 00:05:11.189
Oh my god.

00:05:11.189 --> 00:05:13.189
Yeah, of course.

00:05:13.189 --> 00:05:15.189
What happened?

00:05:15.189 --> 00:05:17.189
Lex just mysteriously disappeared.

00:05:17.189 --> 00:05:20.470
I have to go to Seattle.

00:05:20.470 --> 00:05:22.470
Well, Clark.

00:05:22.470 --> 00:05:24.470
I know that Lex isn't exactly your pick for man of the year,

00:05:24.470 --> 00:05:26.470
but you can't just turn your back on him.

00:05:26.470 --> 00:05:28.470
Chloe, if there's innocent people in danger,

00:05:28.470 --> 00:05:30.470
I'll be back as soon as I can.

00:05:30.470 --> 00:05:39.720
Lex's car's garage, no movement on any financial accounts.

00:05:39.720 --> 00:05:41.720
Airline manifests.

00:05:41.720 --> 00:05:42.720
All negative.

00:05:42.720 --> 00:05:48.790
Well, he can't just have dropped off the face of the earth.

00:05:48.790 --> 00:05:49.790
We have to find him.

00:05:49.790 --> 00:05:54.000
Lana, please.

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:56.000
Come in.

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:59.819
Would you excuse us for a minute?

00:05:59.819 --> 00:06:01.819
Thank you, George.

00:06:01.819 --> 00:06:09.339
Lana, this is just devastating.

00:06:09.339 --> 00:06:12.339
I've taken a sweep for you at the Metro Seasons's hotel.

00:06:12.339 --> 00:06:13.339
It's for your safety.

00:06:13.339 --> 00:06:16.339
For my safety, or to distance me from the cover-up?

00:06:16.339 --> 00:06:19.990
A conspiracy?

00:06:19.990 --> 00:06:22.990
Security refuses to let me see any of the surveillance footage.

00:06:22.990 --> 00:06:23.990
They tell me.

00:06:23.990 --> 00:06:29.509
Tell me that I'm seeing things.

00:06:29.509 --> 00:06:31.509
Tell me. What did you see?

00:06:31.509 --> 00:06:34.509
I don't even know how to begin to explain it.

00:06:34.509 --> 00:06:39.980
But, um, Lex turned into static.

00:06:39.980 --> 00:06:42.980
And then he disappeared.

00:06:42.980 --> 00:06:50.360
It was dark. Perhaps in the chaos.

00:06:50.360 --> 00:06:51.360
I know what I saw.

00:06:51.360 --> 00:06:58.860
Anything that can give me a clue.

00:06:58.860 --> 00:07:00.860
The guards mentioned a number.

00:07:00.860 --> 00:07:01.860
A code.

00:07:01.860 --> 00:07:03.860
1-4-2.

00:07:03.860 --> 00:07:10.120
You know what that means.

00:07:10.120 --> 00:07:12.120
No.

00:07:12.120 --> 00:07:13.120
No, but I will find out.

00:07:13.120 --> 00:07:16.189
But I will find out.

00:07:16.189 --> 00:07:18.430
I am sure you will.

00:07:18.430 --> 00:07:22.430
And I'd appreciate it if you let me know when anything else comes up.

00:07:22.430 --> 00:07:24.430
Of course. I know how important you are, Alex.

00:07:24.430 --> 00:07:41.180
Of course I will.

00:07:41.180 --> 00:07:43.180
Now get me to Dr. Chavez.

00:07:43.180 --> 00:07:45.180
Genome Technology.

00:07:45.180 --> 00:07:59.019
Yeah.

00:07:59.019 --> 00:08:01.019
For all the bodies are counting for?

00:08:01.019 --> 00:08:02.019
It's kind of hard to tell.

00:08:02.019 --> 00:08:04.019
I'll keep you posted.

00:08:17.069 --> 00:08:27.240
You must be the first-year med student I've been waiting for.

00:08:27.240 --> 00:08:33.399
Don't flatline on me now.

00:08:33.399 --> 00:08:35.399
What gave me away?

00:08:35.399 --> 00:08:41.289
A queasy stare that afflicts all newbies their first day on the job.

00:08:41.289 --> 00:08:45.299
You mind?

00:08:45.299 --> 00:08:46.299
How many are there?

00:08:46.299 --> 00:08:48.299
A whole graveyard's worth.

00:08:48.299 --> 00:08:58.870
How does a body end up in one of those?

00:08:58.870 --> 00:09:00.870
I have no skeletons.

00:09:00.870 --> 00:09:05.470
Although I don't know how that's anatomically possible.

00:09:05.470 --> 00:09:07.470
I mean someone cut their bones out?

00:09:07.470 --> 00:09:09.470
More like rip them out.

00:09:09.470 --> 00:09:11.470
Clean filet is every one of them.

00:09:11.470 --> 00:09:15.519
I've seen some stuff that would make most people

00:09:15.519 --> 00:09:17.519
will run for the hills, but this...

00:09:17.519 --> 00:09:19.519
This is seriously freaky.

00:09:19.519 --> 00:09:24.690
All these bodies are from the ship.

00:09:24.690 --> 00:09:30.759
These last two, they were dock workers.

00:09:30.759 --> 00:09:41.120
Whoever was on that ship, it's on dry land now.

00:09:41.120 --> 00:09:50.259
Kid, you puking already?

00:09:50.259 --> 00:09:52.259
Thank God, someone believes me.

00:09:52.259 --> 00:09:54.259
You're the first person who doesn't think I belong in Belarave.

00:09:54.259 --> 00:09:55.259
Lana!

00:09:55.259 --> 00:09:59.259
A lot stranger things have happened in small well.

00:09:59.259 --> 00:10:00.259
Don't worry. We'll find out.

00:10:00.259 --> 00:10:02.259
Lana, thank God you're all right.

00:10:02.259 --> 00:10:05.259
So where exactly those last time is stabilized?

00:10:05.259 --> 00:10:06.259
Um, he was...

00:10:06.259 --> 00:10:08.259
Somewhere in the middle of the room, like around here?

00:10:08.259 --> 00:10:11.259
No. You can't see me.

00:10:11.259 --> 00:10:15.259
You said Lex backs up all of his security footage on an internal server, right?

00:10:15.259 --> 00:10:16.259
Yeah, I think so.

00:10:16.259 --> 00:10:18.259
Okay, we're gonna need a password.

00:10:18.259 --> 00:10:20.259
Even one likes are close. Are you password close?

00:10:20.259 --> 00:10:22.259
No, I guess not.

00:10:22.259 --> 00:10:25.259
Lana. The password is your birthday.

00:10:25.259 --> 00:10:29.259
Why don't you try a Julian? His brother or Lily and his mom?

00:10:29.259 --> 00:10:30.259
Your birthday.

00:10:30.259 --> 00:10:38.990
X-Nay. Okay, how about Lana?

00:10:38.990 --> 00:10:40.990
No. You have anything else?

00:10:40.990 --> 00:10:41.990
No, I don't know.

00:10:41.990 --> 00:10:42.990
Damn it!

00:10:42.990 --> 00:10:43.990
Don't worry.

00:10:43.990 --> 00:10:45.990
We'll just upload the whole hard drive.

00:10:45.990 --> 00:10:47.990
And I'll work on it later.

00:10:47.990 --> 00:10:49.990
Chloe, the way he disappeared.

00:10:49.990 --> 00:10:50.990
What if...

00:10:50.990 --> 00:10:54.720
What if Lex is really gone?

00:10:54.720 --> 00:10:58.320
Forever?

00:10:58.320 --> 00:11:00.320
Don't worry. I'll find my way back to you.

00:11:00.320 --> 00:11:02.320
You can't think that way, Lana.

00:11:02.320 --> 00:11:04.320
We're gonna get him back.

00:11:04.320 --> 00:11:07.320
I've had so many doubts about this relationship.

00:11:07.320 --> 00:11:09.320
So many suspicions.

00:11:09.320 --> 00:11:13.080
But now that he's gone, none of it matters anymore.

00:11:13.080 --> 00:11:15.080
Just want to see his face again.

00:11:15.080 --> 00:11:19.340
again.

00:11:19.340 --> 00:11:25.309
I love you so much.

00:11:25.309 --> 00:11:27.309
I'll crack this back to The Daily Planet.

00:11:27.309 --> 00:11:28.309
And either we'll get a week's worth of

00:11:28.309 --> 00:11:30.309
Lex sipping bourbon and dizzling on his computer,

00:11:30.309 --> 00:11:33.309
or we'll actually hit the jackpot.

00:11:33.309 --> 00:11:35.309
Lana, wait, don't go.

00:11:35.309 --> 00:11:37.309
How's it feel, Lex?

00:11:37.309 --> 00:11:40.940
Have your whole life ripped from under you?

00:11:40.940 --> 00:11:46.230
I know you.

00:11:46.230 --> 00:11:48.700
Don't you?

00:11:48.700 --> 00:11:49.700
You should.

00:11:49.700 --> 00:11:51.700
You saw my face through the observation window.

00:11:51.700 --> 00:12:10.830
You're the one for, too.

00:12:10.830 --> 00:12:12.830
I know that Lex Luther lost is a juicy headline,

00:12:12.830 --> 00:12:14.830
but tell me again why we're searching for the root of all evil.

00:12:14.830 --> 00:12:15.830
I'm not doing.

00:12:15.830 --> 00:12:16.830
This for Lex.

00:12:16.830 --> 00:12:19.830
After talking to Lana, I've got to put my skepticism in check.

00:12:19.830 --> 00:12:21.830
I mean, she really cares about him.

00:12:21.830 --> 00:12:24.830
Women are such a mystery.

00:12:24.830 --> 00:12:26.830
Finding Lex is a bigger mystery.

00:12:26.830 --> 00:12:28.830
Where's Clark when we need him?

00:12:28.830 --> 00:12:30.830
What does Clark have to do with anything?

00:12:30.830 --> 00:12:33.830
Look, I know that you feel sore for the guy because he's always flying solo,

00:12:33.830 --> 00:12:35.830
but honestly, what can that guy do that I can't?

00:12:35.830 --> 00:12:38.830
You know, you're probably right.

00:12:38.830 --> 00:12:41.830
Betcha you wouldn't brave the rush hour crunch just to get your favorite bending machine cuisine,

00:12:41.830 --> 00:12:44.830
all so that you can have time to continue the hunt for a man that nobody misses while.

00:12:44.830 --> 00:12:46.830
Nobody misses, well, maybe except...

00:12:46.830 --> 00:12:47.830
Lana!

00:12:47.830 --> 00:12:51.500
The hunt for Lex is on.

00:12:51.500 --> 00:12:54.500
Can I get you anything from the basement buffet?

00:12:54.500 --> 00:12:58.159
Thank you, but I'm okay.

00:12:58.159 --> 00:13:00.159
So, I do have some good news.

00:13:00.159 --> 00:13:02.159
I managed to stumble on the magic password,

00:13:02.159 --> 00:13:06.159
and it turns out to be none other than the birthday of Miss Lana Lane.

00:13:06.159 --> 00:13:09.159
I was able to access the surveillance files, and look what I dug up.

00:13:09.159 --> 00:13:19.990
There's something there.

00:13:19.990 --> 00:13:23.779
Can you make it any clear?

00:13:23.779 --> 00:13:25.779
I'm doing my best, but I don't have a lot to work with.

00:13:25.779 --> 00:13:33.350
It's going to take some time.

00:13:33.350 --> 00:13:34.350
Hello?

00:13:34.350 --> 00:13:36.350
I know what happened to Lex Luthor.

00:13:36.350 --> 00:13:38.350
Who is this?

00:13:38.350 --> 00:13:41.350
If anyone knows we're talking, we're both in danger.

00:13:41.350 --> 00:13:43.919
What's wrong?

00:13:43.919 --> 00:13:48.580
It's just Lex's security. They want to give me an update.

00:13:48.580 --> 00:14:07.190
Did anyone follow you here?

00:14:07.190 --> 00:14:11.190
No. Please, what happened to Lex?

00:14:11.190 --> 00:14:12.190
I took him.

00:14:12.190 --> 00:14:15.190
And if you ever want to see him again, you'll keep your mouth shut

00:14:15.190 --> 00:14:18.190
and listen to exactly what I have to say.

00:14:18.190 --> 00:14:21.190
Whatever you want, just don't hurt him.

00:14:21.190 --> 00:14:24.190
You know your boyfriend has a secret lab hidden inside Luther court?

00:14:24.190 --> 00:14:28.190
tower called 33.1. Why is it secret?

00:14:28.190 --> 00:14:32.190
Because they run experiments on the people who have been infected by the meteorops.

00:14:32.190 --> 00:14:38.190
When patients are released from Villaree, instead of a freedom, they get a one-way ticket to a secret laboratory.

00:14:38.190 --> 00:14:41.190
How do you know all this?

00:14:41.190 --> 00:14:43.190
Because I was one of them.

00:14:43.190 --> 00:14:45.190
Until I broke out last night.

00:14:45.190 --> 00:14:48.190
Why should I believe you?

00:14:48.190 --> 00:14:53.190
See, that's the point. Nobody believes me. I'm a former mental patient.

00:14:53.190 --> 00:14:54.190
But you?

00:14:54.190 --> 00:14:57.190
You, you're your Lex's beloved girlfriend.

00:14:57.190 --> 00:14:59.190
Once you blow the whistle on this place,

00:14:59.190 --> 00:15:01.190
people will have to listen, right?

00:15:01.190 --> 00:15:03.190
Where's the evidence?

00:15:03.190 --> 00:15:06.629
You don't have any proof?

00:15:06.629 --> 00:15:07.629
Of course I do.

00:15:07.629 --> 00:15:13.220
I can take you that.

00:15:13.220 --> 00:15:15.220
You can see for yourself.

00:15:15.220 --> 00:15:20.450
And then you'll release Lex?

00:15:20.450 --> 00:15:36.500
Hey, this area's off limits.

00:15:36.500 --> 00:15:39.500
Um, with the coroner's office?

00:15:39.500 --> 00:15:41.500
Better you than me.

00:15:41.500 --> 00:15:44.500
I heard the bodies are pretty messed up.

00:15:44.500 --> 00:15:46.500
Anyway, our theory is the body is a pretty messed up.

00:15:46.500 --> 00:15:48.500
Herf was hiding out in this container.

00:15:48.500 --> 00:15:50.500
He somehow busted out of this thing.

00:15:50.500 --> 00:15:52.500
He started his killing stroke. It's wild.

00:15:52.500 --> 00:15:56.000
We thought it was blood.

00:15:56.000 --> 00:15:58.000
But the guys are saying it's human bone marrow.

00:15:58.000 --> 00:16:03.580
It's frickin disgusting.

00:16:03.580 --> 00:16:05.580
Actually, there are a few more remains in the removal.

00:16:05.580 --> 00:16:07.580
The French team is over there waiting for you.

00:16:07.580 --> 00:16:09.580
Thanks. Sure.

00:16:09.580 --> 00:16:41.500
One who's hungry.

00:16:41.500 --> 00:17:04.500
You were infected by the meteors?

00:17:07.500 --> 00:17:09.500
I was an electrician.

00:17:09.500 --> 00:17:14.500
I was working up in a radio tower last year when the meteors hit.

00:17:14.500 --> 00:17:16.500
I got thrown off.

00:17:16.500 --> 00:17:20.500
And somehow I ended up with an ability.

00:17:20.500 --> 00:17:28.940
I can move through alternate frequencies.

00:17:28.940 --> 00:17:36.019
I can shift into planes of existence that nobody knows exists.

00:17:36.019 --> 00:17:43.150
Hey, if you think I'm strange, wait till you see some of the other people on this floor.

00:17:43.150 --> 00:17:47.150
Aren't you afraid they're just going to grab you the minute those doors open?

00:17:47.150 --> 00:17:54.319
If I have to sacrifice myself to get the truth out, then so be it.

00:17:54.319 --> 00:18:06.910
The fact is they're not going to grab you.

00:18:06.910 --> 00:18:28.339
I understand. This is wrong.

00:18:28.339 --> 00:18:35.339
wrong. It was here. 24 hours ago, it was all here. The holding cells, the labs.

00:18:35.339 --> 00:18:37.339
Take me to Lex.

00:18:37.339 --> 00:18:40.339
What did that bastard do with everyone?

00:18:40.339 --> 00:18:46.339
I know that you believe that something was here, but clearly, nothing's been here for a long time.

00:18:46.339 --> 00:18:48.339
I'm telling you it was here!

00:18:48.339 --> 00:18:52.339
Okay. Just relax. We'll figure out where everything was moved to.

00:18:52.339 --> 00:18:55.339
But first, I need you to tell me what you've done with Lex.

00:18:55.339 --> 00:19:00.150
I put him in a place where he can't hurt anyone else.

00:19:00.150 --> 00:19:18.500
He can't hurt anyone else.

00:19:18.500 --> 00:19:21.500
What did you do with 33.1?

00:19:21.500 --> 00:19:23.500
I didn't do anything.

00:19:23.500 --> 00:19:25.500
I think it's pretty obvious I haven't gone anywhere.

00:19:25.500 --> 00:19:27.500
Don't lie to me.

00:19:27.500 --> 00:19:29.500
It's the truth.

00:19:29.500 --> 00:19:31.500
The truth.

00:19:31.500 --> 00:19:36.500
The truth is you kept me locked up in a concrete bunker

00:19:36.500 --> 00:19:38.500
just when I was about to go back to a normal life.

00:19:38.500 --> 00:19:41.849
Normal life.

00:19:41.849 --> 00:19:44.849
You were never going to be released from Belle Reeve.

00:19:44.849 --> 00:19:46.849
It was a figment of your fractured.

00:19:46.849 --> 00:19:47.849
And I was...

00:19:47.849 --> 00:19:49.349
I was trying to help you.

00:19:49.349 --> 00:19:53.039
Other patients!

00:19:53.039 --> 00:19:57.470
If I knew, don't you think I'd tell you?

00:19:57.470 --> 00:19:59.470
I didn't want to have to resort to violence, Lex.

00:19:59.470 --> 00:20:01.470
You're not giving me much of a choice here.

00:20:01.470 --> 00:20:02.470
Okay.

00:20:02.470 --> 00:20:07.309
Calm down.

00:20:07.309 --> 00:20:10.910
Maybe when I bring Lana here?

00:20:10.910 --> 00:20:11.910
We'll see if you talk.

00:20:11.910 --> 00:20:24.750
Wow.

00:20:24.750 --> 00:20:29.250
You were a gadget junkie, but this stuff looks like it's from the Jurassic era.

00:20:29.250 --> 00:20:30.750
Well, when I heard about Mr. Frequency Jumper,

00:20:30.750 --> 00:20:33.250
I decided to dust off my pop's old ham radio equipment.

00:20:33.250 --> 00:20:34.250
Ham radio?

00:20:34.250 --> 00:20:37.750
Yeah, people were communicating worldwide long before the internet existed.

00:20:37.750 --> 00:20:39.750
I used to sneak downstairs into the late night airway.

00:20:39.750 --> 00:20:43.750
late-night airwaves. My handle, Jimmy, the infuriator.

00:20:43.750 --> 00:20:45.750
Why does that not surprise me?

00:20:45.750 --> 00:20:49.750
Alright, just listen carefully, girls.

00:20:49.750 --> 00:20:51.750
Password.

00:20:51.750 --> 00:20:58.299
Right there. Okay, did you hear that?

00:20:58.299 --> 00:21:00.299
How could you not?

00:21:00.299 --> 00:21:03.299
That's a radio frequency. And after scanning all the footage, that sound kept coming back.

00:21:03.299 --> 00:21:07.299
So I tried blending the narrow band frequency modulation with the UHF modulation.

00:21:07.299 --> 00:21:13.490
Okay, just here, check this up.

00:21:13.490 --> 00:21:27.109
Lex was in the room and you just couldn't hear it.

00:21:27.109 --> 00:21:28.109
Or see him.

00:21:28.109 --> 00:21:39.890
Oh, my God.

00:21:39.890 --> 00:21:44.480
He heard everything I said.

00:21:44.480 --> 00:21:46.480
Look, this may sound absurd,

00:21:46.480 --> 00:21:49.480
but I think that Lex may be trapped in another frequency.

00:21:49.480 --> 00:21:54.140
Okay, kind of like radio.

00:21:54.140 --> 00:21:57.140
The way AM and FM are different frequencies,

00:21:57.140 --> 00:21:58.140
but they move to the same space.

00:21:58.140 --> 00:22:01.140
Can we communicate with him?

00:22:01.140 --> 00:22:03.140
It seems to be some sort of frequency loop in the library,

00:22:03.140 --> 00:22:06.140
so as long as you're in that room, it might be possible.

00:22:06.140 --> 00:22:51.079
Let's try.

00:22:51.079 --> 00:22:54.609
You escape from the phantom zone.

00:22:54.609 --> 00:22:56.609
But I'm no phantom.

00:22:56.609 --> 00:23:41.309
I think it must be some kind of a glitch or...

00:23:41.309 --> 00:23:46.309
I don't know much about this stuff, but I do know that, excuse me,

00:23:46.309 --> 00:23:52.309
that when you hack into a secure operating system,

00:23:52.309 --> 00:23:56.309
you could pick up some very nasty viruses.

00:23:56.309 --> 00:23:58.309
I guess I better take that to heart.

00:23:58.309 --> 00:24:00.750
Miss Sullivan.

00:24:00.750 --> 00:24:04.750
Luther Corp considers any breach of security of very serious matter,

00:24:04.750 --> 00:24:05.750
and you know that.

00:24:05.750 --> 00:24:06.750
that.

00:24:06.750 --> 00:24:07.750
Mr. Luther, I'm trying to find your son.

00:24:07.750 --> 00:24:08.750
I appreciate that.

00:24:08.750 --> 00:24:12.750
In fact, I was hoping, being the diligent reporter you are,

00:24:12.750 --> 00:24:14.750
that you could provide a clue that would help me to find Lex.

00:24:14.750 --> 00:24:19.750
Well, the only clue I have is a little lab called 33.1,

00:24:19.750 --> 00:24:22.750
otherwise known as Meteor Freaks Central?

00:24:22.750 --> 00:24:24.750
I was always under the impression that...

00:24:24.750 --> 00:24:25.750
Meteor Freaks?

00:24:25.750 --> 00:24:28.750
You're not in high school anymore, Miss Sullivan.

00:24:28.750 --> 00:24:29.750
This is the real world.

00:24:29.750 --> 00:24:30.750
Please.

00:24:30.750 --> 00:24:43.529
His daddy Warbucks is doing here.

00:24:43.529 --> 00:24:45.529
I know Luther just ransacked all of my research.

00:24:45.529 --> 00:24:46.529
of my research.

00:24:46.529 --> 00:24:51.759
Then I were back to square one.

00:24:51.759 --> 00:24:56.329
Maybe not square one, more like triangle one.

00:24:56.329 --> 00:24:58.329
Jimmy, what's up?

00:24:58.329 --> 00:25:00.329
Triangulation.

00:25:00.329 --> 00:25:03.329
I might actually have a way of squeaking Lex out of that frequency.

00:25:03.329 --> 00:25:16.720
Lex, I know you're here.

00:25:16.720 --> 00:25:20.930
Hopefully you can hear me.

00:25:20.930 --> 00:25:23.930
Because there's something that I...

00:25:23.930 --> 00:25:33.359
I've been so focused on our problems

00:25:33.359 --> 00:25:40.470
that I have lost sight of how much you really mean to me.

00:25:40.470 --> 00:25:42.470
These times I was reluctant to trust you.

00:25:42.470 --> 00:25:57.039
The fact is more honest with me than anyone's ever been.

00:25:57.039 --> 00:25:58.039
I miss you so much.

00:25:58.039 --> 00:26:03.819
I don't know what I do without you.

00:26:03.819 --> 00:26:11.519
I love you, Lex.

00:26:11.519 --> 00:26:16.640
I love you too, Anna.

00:26:16.640 --> 00:26:24.880
Please don't leave us here.

00:26:24.880 --> 00:26:27.880
I don't want to have this baby without you.

00:26:27.880 --> 00:26:34.230
I should have told you.

00:26:34.230 --> 00:26:46.430
You are here.

00:26:46.430 --> 00:26:50.859
You're sorry to have to put you through this.

00:26:50.859 --> 00:26:57.029
Mother, you tell me where you moved 33.1.

00:26:57.029 --> 00:27:01.029
But you can say goodbye to Lana Lang.

00:27:01.029 --> 00:27:11.019
Whatever Lex is done in the past.

00:27:11.019 --> 00:27:13.019
Lex has done in the past, I'll make him stop.

00:27:13.019 --> 00:27:15.019
He'll listen to me.

00:27:15.019 --> 00:27:16.019
You hear that, Lex?

00:27:16.019 --> 00:27:18.019
Even to love your life wants you to come clean

00:27:18.019 --> 00:27:19.019
and tell the world what you've done.

00:27:19.019 --> 00:27:21.460
Let her go.

00:27:21.460 --> 00:27:23.460
You can see him.

00:27:23.460 --> 00:27:25.460
Where is 33.1?

00:27:25.460 --> 00:27:27.460
I told you, I don't know!

00:27:27.460 --> 00:27:29.460
Now let's go over!

00:27:29.460 --> 00:27:32.349
Let's go over!

00:27:32.349 --> 00:27:35.349
Let's get started.

00:27:35.349 --> 00:27:47.730
Why do you think they call me Jimmy the Infuriator?

00:27:47.730 --> 00:27:49.730
Lex is a dead man?

00:27:49.730 --> 00:27:51.730
Don't let him get away.

00:27:51.730 --> 00:27:52.730
He's not going anywhere.

00:27:52.730 --> 00:27:56.079
Where is Lex?

00:27:56.079 --> 00:27:58.079
What's the frequency?

00:27:58.079 --> 00:28:06.980
That can't be a good thing.

00:28:06.980 --> 00:28:08.980
We need that radio frequency jammer now.

00:28:08.980 --> 00:28:13.410
I think I'm picking up in so far.

00:28:13.410 --> 00:28:25.009
She wanted to say goodbye in person.

00:28:25.009 --> 00:28:31.059
I agree.

00:28:31.059 --> 00:28:33.059
Whatever frequency they don't have to jam that exact signal.

00:28:33.059 --> 00:28:35.059
So what's the problem? Do it?

00:28:35.059 --> 00:28:36.059
Sure, no problem.

00:28:36.059 --> 00:28:38.059
There's a gazillion to sort there.

00:28:38.059 --> 00:28:46.539
It gets across, I'll call.

00:28:46.539 --> 00:29:01.220
I can't too much of food.

00:29:01.220 --> 00:29:02.220
Do you?

00:29:02.220 --> 00:29:03.220
Jimmy, hurry.

00:29:03.220 --> 00:29:21.119
Pooley, hear it?

00:29:21.119 --> 00:29:22.119
Let's go.

00:29:22.119 --> 00:29:28.210
Lana.

00:29:28.210 --> 00:29:36.859
You're okay.

00:29:36.859 --> 00:29:42.029
I had to find you.

00:29:42.029 --> 00:29:47.549
I'd rather be trapped here with you

00:29:47.549 --> 00:29:49.549
than I'll see you again.

00:29:49.549 --> 00:29:50.549
Come here.

00:29:50.549 --> 00:29:58.109
Come on.

00:29:58.109 --> 00:30:01.250
Do you.

00:30:01.250 --> 00:30:10.730
Everything.

00:30:10.730 --> 00:30:11.730
Bypass the oscillator and go direct.

00:30:11.730 --> 00:30:13.730
You're trying to crease in the injury.

00:30:13.730 --> 00:31:12.279
Blood must make you strong.

00:31:12.279 --> 00:31:14.279
I should taste it.

00:31:14.279 --> 00:31:20.789
Why are you doing this?

00:31:20.789 --> 00:31:22.789
Everyone's got to eat.

00:31:22.789 --> 00:32:00.960
That was you, wasn't it?

00:32:00.960 --> 00:32:30.960
Typical form.

00:32:30.960 --> 00:32:33.960
There's enough power pumping in here to light up Metropolis.

00:32:33.960 --> 00:32:36.960
Something tells me it wasn't just for the fluorescent lights.

00:32:36.960 --> 00:32:42.519
It's just a matter of time until I get to the bottom of it.

00:32:42.519 --> 00:32:46.519
You really manned up and got right into this fight.

00:32:46.519 --> 00:32:49.519
I still wish Clark was here to help?

00:32:49.519 --> 00:32:53.519
Oh, come on. Clark can't hold a candle to the infuriator.

00:32:53.519 --> 00:32:57.519
Hey, find anything interesting?

00:32:57.519 --> 00:33:00.690
Yeah.

00:33:00.690 --> 00:33:03.690
I gotta say, this all just feels a little strange.

00:33:03.690 --> 00:33:07.690
Have you ever considered the possibility that maybe Bronson is telling the truth?

00:33:07.690 --> 00:33:12.640
And this was some secret laboratory?

00:33:12.640 --> 00:33:17.640
Chloe, I don't think Lex would have given us clearance if he had something to hide.

00:33:17.640 --> 00:33:22.640
It seems like a lot of hoops for someone bent on revenge to jump through if 33.1 never even existed.

00:33:22.640 --> 00:33:24.640
Chloe, the guy was delusional.

00:33:24.640 --> 00:33:26.640
The meteor exposure made him sick.

00:33:26.640 --> 00:33:28.640
He spent over a year in Belrieve.

00:33:28.640 --> 00:33:31.640
There's a lot more to this story than meets the eye.

00:33:31.640 --> 00:33:32.640
You don't know that.

00:33:32.640 --> 00:33:33.640
the Luthers like I do.

00:33:33.640 --> 00:33:36.640
You don't know Lex like I do.

00:33:36.640 --> 00:33:42.940
I'm not going to take the word of a homicidal maniac over Lex.

00:33:42.940 --> 00:33:43.940
I'm sorry.

00:33:43.940 --> 00:33:47.940
Lana, you can't prove that 33.1 didn't exist.

00:33:47.940 --> 00:33:49.940
And you can't prove that it did.

00:33:49.940 --> 00:34:15.570
It says on the door out there that this is my office,

00:34:15.570 --> 00:34:17.570
my private office.

00:34:17.570 --> 00:34:19.570
Obviously, that doesn't mean much to you.

00:34:19.570 --> 00:34:22.570
You interfered with a project you have nothing to do with.

00:34:22.570 --> 00:34:26.570
Oh, you must be talking about, uh, what do you call it, 33.1?

00:34:26.570 --> 00:34:30.070
3.1. You should thank me for coming to the rescue.

00:34:30.070 --> 00:34:34.570
I'd hate to think of the legal repercussions if that clinic was discovered.

00:34:34.570 --> 00:34:38.570
Not to speak of the dirt that would stick to our corporate image.

00:34:38.570 --> 00:34:43.679
You did this for selfish reasons.

00:34:43.679 --> 00:34:47.679
Your fascination with the meteor infected started long before mine.

00:34:47.679 --> 00:34:52.679
But you have gone farther with a scientific experiment

00:34:52.679 --> 00:34:55.679
than I ever believed was possible.

00:34:55.679 --> 00:34:57.679
Congratulations. Kudos, son. I'm proud.

00:34:57.679 --> 00:35:02.079
Son, I'm proud of you.

00:35:02.079 --> 00:35:04.079
Your methods are a tad disappointing.

00:35:04.079 --> 00:35:12.980
You've still got a lot to learn when it comes to the fine art of secrecy.

00:35:12.980 --> 00:35:14.980
What did you do at 33.1?

00:35:14.980 --> 00:35:16.980
Moved it.

00:35:16.980 --> 00:35:18.980
The whole shebang.

00:35:18.980 --> 00:35:22.710
To a top security location.

00:35:22.710 --> 00:35:24.710
Happy to let you have the coordinates.

00:35:24.710 --> 00:35:28.239
Just one condition.

00:35:28.239 --> 00:35:31.610
And what might that be?

00:35:31.610 --> 00:35:33.610
Make me your full partner.

00:35:33.610 --> 00:35:35.610
I want to know everything about this project.

00:35:35.610 --> 00:35:41.489
It's a chance to spend more quality time together.

00:35:41.489 --> 00:35:54.929
So what? Your cell phone doesn't get

00:35:54.949 --> 00:35:56.949
reception in Seattle?

00:35:56.949 --> 00:35:58.949
I was preoccupied.

00:35:58.949 --> 00:36:01.949
That's fine. But you were up against an alien from another planet.

00:36:01.949 --> 00:36:02.949
I was worried.

00:36:02.949 --> 00:36:07.219
I'm sorry.

00:36:07.219 --> 00:36:09.219
So the crystal was a success?

00:36:09.219 --> 00:36:19.969
Then did the zoner just decide to pack up and leave the solar system?

00:36:19.969 --> 00:36:22.969
Someone else killed him.

00:36:22.969 --> 00:36:26.969
Someone who can do things I could only dream of.

00:36:26.969 --> 00:36:28.969
Whoa.

00:36:28.969 --> 00:36:31.969
So there's someone he's on our side, right?

00:36:31.969 --> 00:36:34.599
I'm not sure.

00:36:34.599 --> 00:36:36.599
Clerk, it's me.

00:36:36.599 --> 00:36:39.599
Your most trusted friend and secret keeper?

00:36:39.599 --> 00:36:41.599
How about a few details?

00:36:41.599 --> 00:36:44.599
Believe it or not, there are some things you don't need to know.

00:36:44.599 --> 00:36:50.269
Look, I understand that you feel like all these psychopathic space invaders are your fault,

00:36:50.269 --> 00:36:53.269
but you can't keep it all inside.

00:36:53.269 --> 00:36:57.269
You feel the need to carry the world on your shoulders, and that's noble.

00:36:57.269 --> 00:37:01.269
But there are other people out there who want to help you fight the good fight,

00:37:01.269 --> 00:37:07.300
and you need to let them in.

00:37:07.300 --> 00:37:09.300
Because sometimes even heroes need to be saved.

00:37:09.300 --> 00:37:52.679
You should be off your feet.

00:37:52.679 --> 00:37:53.679
Here.

00:37:53.679 --> 00:37:54.679
Sit out.

00:37:54.679 --> 00:37:55.679
Can I get you something in your training?

00:37:55.679 --> 00:37:57.679
Legs. I'm pregnant. I'm not an invalid.

00:37:57.679 --> 00:37:59.679
I'm sorry.

00:37:59.679 --> 00:38:02.679
I just want to make things perfect for you.

00:38:02.679 --> 00:38:04.679
I'm sorry.

00:38:04.679 --> 00:38:07.679
I had no right to keep this a secret.

00:38:07.679 --> 00:38:11.960
I wanted to tell you. I just...

00:38:11.960 --> 00:38:13.960
I wasn't sure.

00:38:13.960 --> 00:38:14.960
With how I'd react?

00:38:14.960 --> 00:38:22.090
It's the best news I've ever heard.

00:38:22.090 --> 00:38:31.739
One one I love is carrying my child.

00:38:31.739 --> 00:38:37.440
My child. Our child. What more could a man want?

00:38:37.440 --> 00:38:53.260
Listen, Lex, um, about this 33.1 place.

00:38:53.260 --> 00:38:58.440
I already told you. It never existed.

00:38:58.440 --> 00:39:08.159
But if it did, I understand why.

00:39:08.159 --> 00:39:12.159
These people who've been infected by the meteors are dangerous.

00:39:12.159 --> 00:39:15.159
They've hurt me and they've hurt people that I care about.

00:39:15.159 --> 00:39:21.010
The more we learn about them, the better we can protect ourselves.

00:39:21.010 --> 00:39:27.590
And there's something else you need to know.

00:39:27.590 --> 00:39:29.590
Thank you.

